BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (OFS data blocks include a 24-byte header with block type, ownership, sequence and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (checksum-related fields before the payload. File header and extension blocks carry pointers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (to data blocks, timestamps, names and comments. Root and directory header blocks maintain) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (directory hash-chain links. Free and used blocks are tracked in on-media bitmap blocks, not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (in a FAT-style next-cluster table.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (Amiga filesystems use block keys and structured blocks with checksums. The DOS type in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (boot block identifies variant features. Header tables can point to data blocks in an order) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (different from physical placement; reverse-oriented pointer tables and extension blocks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (must be interpreted according to the upstream format. Logical payload size is not simply) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 512.0 Tm (equal to the number of allocated blocks times the block size, because OFS data block) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 495.0 Tm (headers consume space.) Tj ET
