BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (The root block and directory headers act as directories containing hashed link chains to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (child objects. Names, Amiga protection bits, comments and datestamps belong to on-disk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (entry metadata. File extension blocks are required when the direct header's pointer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (capacity is exceeded. Different DOS variants add changes to the name comparison, directory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (cache and long-name representation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (Bitmap state identifies free blocks, but consistency also requires traversing every rooted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (object and tracing every referenced header, extension and data block. Filesystems may) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (contain hard and symbolic link concepts that differ from Unix, and modern Linux adapters) Tj ET
