BT /F2 16 Tf 0.02 0.44 0.50 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (INTEGRITY, VALIDATION AND RECOVERY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 677.0 Tm (OFS protects its structural and file data blocks with on-media checksums, unlike FFS data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 660.0 Tm (blocks. The checksums detect many forms of corruption but do not supply modern) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 643.0 Tm (transactional rollback. The volume may also have bitmap-valid state and must not be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 626.0 Tm (declared writable after an interrupted update without checking allocation ownership and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 609.0 Tm (structural reachability.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 580.0 Tm (Safe recovery requires checking root and directory structures, bitmap ownership, extension) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 563.0 Tm (chains, data-sequence numbers, header checksums and links. A bitmap rebuild is acceptable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 546.0 Tm (only if the file tree provides an internally consistent ownership inventory. Failure during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 529.0 Tm (metadata changes can leave seemingly valid blocks with inconsistent higher-level ownership;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.2 Tf 0.09 0.16 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 51 512.0 Tm (inventing a missing parent risks permanent damage.) Tj ET
